  "coder_notes": "§4.1.1 gives a 9:0.5:0.5 train/val/test split only for the 2000-image rail surface micro-crack dataset (item 1), not for NEU-DET (item 2). Table 2 only lists hardware and software versions without training hyperparameters (epochs, batch size, learning rate, input resolution). Table 5 evaluates ZoomHead across YOLOv10n/s/m/b/l/x and YOLO11n/s/m/l/x on NEU-DET (highest mAP@50 is YOLO11l-ZoomHead at 77.9% vs 76.5% for YOLO11l; YOLOv10n-ZoomHead achieves 76.7% vs 73.5% for YOLOv10n). Note an internal discrepancy between Table 5 (YOLO11n-ZoomHead mAP@50 = 0.762) and Table 11 (YOLOv11n-ZoomHead mAP@50 = 0.772, while text §4.4.2 says YOLO11n-ZoomHead is slightly inferior to YOLO11n-DyHead at 0.755, likely a typo in Table 11)."
